under `crawler/`. Their README files describe the changes against the original.

matcher/algorithms/graph/data/mesh-terms.json.gz contains an adapted subset of
Medical Subject Headings (MeSH), 2026, U.S. National Library of Medicine.
Terms: https://www.nlm.nih.gov/databases/download/terms_and_conditions_mesh.html
German MeSH 2026, ZB MED – Information Centre for Life Sciences,
https://repository.publisso.de/resource/frl:6529716, CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The matcher extracts English and
German terms, disease descendants and the kind of a procedure, and adds German
clinical name forms of neoplasms by site. It includes WHO code-to-MeSH retrieval
IDs derived from the Mondo 2026-11-03 exact mapping sets, CC0 1.0,
https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/tree/v2026-11-03/src/ontology/mappings.
